  "correction_rules": [
    "Adjust forecasts downward when sentiment history shows sustained negative sentiment (e.g., multiple -0.25 or 0.00 values), indicating market pessimism.",
    "Reduce forecast peaks after sharp spikes — model tends to overreact; apply a 1-2 day lag correction to avoid overshoot.",
    "When sentiment includes 0.50 or 0.67, model often overestimates upward momentum; apply a 10-15% downward bias to prevent overconfidence.",
    "For 30-day forecasts, if true outcome deviates >10% from 15-day moving average, apply mean reversion correction toward recent trend.",
    "If forecast is consistently below true outcome over 3 consecutive days, increase forecast by 2-5% to align with upward momentum.",
    "When sentiment history includes 0.00 for 5+ days, model tends to underreact — increase forecast slightly to capture delayed rebound."
  ]
